load @term/seed/machine/turing
  find turing-machine

# Universality: the existence of a single machine that, given the description of any machine and its input, simulates
# it. A universal Turing machine runs any program, which is why one computer can run all software. Universality is
# common, appearing in tiny cellular automata and simple rewrite systems, and the substrate is universal: its one
# reversible rule can simulate any computation. The form carries the Turing machine being simulated; the universal
# machine is the one that reads its description.
form universal-machine
  link machine, like turing-machine
